# Collection admission: defer generic iterator dictionaries to callers
#
# A generic collector's iterator dictionary (a trait clause of the function,
# possibly projected through parent clauses) becomes an obligation of the
# function. Every call instantiates the callee's obligations and checks them
# against the reviewed iterators, or defers them to the caller's clauses, to a
# fixpoint. Also admits the modeled BTreeMap/BTreeSet Extend and the BTreeSet
# Iter/IntoIter iterators.

